.TH BYTE_DIFF2 3
.SH NAME
byte_diff2 \- compare two byte arrays of different lengths
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "int byte_diff2(const char* " a ", size_t " alen ", const char* " b ", size_t " blen ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_diff2
performs a lexicographical comparison between the byte array
.I a
of length
.I alen
and the byte array
.I b
of length
.IR blen .
.PP
The comparison logic is as follows:
.IP \(bu 3
If
.I alen
is less than
.IR blen ,
the result is negative (specifically, the negation of the byte at
.I b[alen]
).
.IP \(bu 3
If
.I blen
is less than
.IR alen ,
the result is positive (specifically, the byte at
.I a[blen]
).
.IP \(bu 3
If the lengths are equal, it delegates the comparison to
.BR byte_diff (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a negative value if
.I a
is lexicographically smaller than
.IR b ,
zero if they are equal, or a positive value if
.I a
is greater than
.IR b .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR byte_diff (3),
.BR str_diff (3)